1
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:07,480
Buona sera, Luigi's Pizza.

2
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:08,830
Buona sera.

3
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:11,120
It means good evening in Italian.

4
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:14,350
May I say, having to explain that to you calls into question

5
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,670
the authenticity of your ristorante?

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,730
Okay, I'm out of here.

7
00:00:19,730 --> 00:00:20,980
Un momento.

8
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:22,760
Oh, for heaven's sake.

9
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:24,570
Now you're being deliberately stupid.

10
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:26,900
Where are you going?

11
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,690
I'm having dinner with Priya at Raj's.

12
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:30,640
I think Howard's going to be there. You want to join us?

13
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:31,990
But tonight's Thursday.

14
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:33,990
On Thursdays, everybody comes over here

15
00:00:33,990 --> 00:00:35,080
and has pizza.

16
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,010
Or a reasonable facsimile

17
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:39,140
prepared by someone claiming to be Luigi,

18
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:41,670
but who sounds suspiciously like Jackie Chan.

19
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,570
Can't we make a one-time exception for tonight?

20
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:46,620
We could.

21
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:49,260
We could also stop using the letter "M,"

22
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:52,410
but I think that idea is isguided and oronic.

23
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:55,100
Just come with me to Raj's.

24
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,750
Well, I don't want to go to a party.

25
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,620
It's not a party. It's the same group of people

26
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:00,510
who hang out here hanging out over there.

27
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:04,470
I'm sorry, but five people eating and chatting is a party.

28
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:07,050
How come it's not a party when we do it here?

29
00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:08,800
Because we don't throw parties.

30
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:10,940
I don't know what to tell you, Sheldon.

31
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:12,620
I'm going to see Priya. Everyone's over there.

32
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:13,410
You coming or not?

33
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:15,880
Well, no, sir, and do you know why?

34
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:16,920
In a word:

35
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,110
tradition.

36
00:01:18,690 --> 00:01:21,200
Every Thursday night for the last eight years,

37
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,900
you and I and our friends have gathered here

38
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:28,220
in this very spot to break bread covered with cheese and sauce,

39
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:30,070
discuss the issues of the day,

40
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,350
and yes, share a laugh or two.

41
00:01:33,390 --> 00:01:36,830
But I guess our rich heritage means nothing to you.

42
00:01:37,270 --> 00:01:37,890
I guess you're right.

43
00:01:37,890 --> 00:01:38,910
- See you later. - Wait!

44
00:01:38,910 --> 00:01:40,950
Leonard! Wait!

45
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:42,450
What am I going to do for dinner?

46
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:44,470
Come with me to Raj's and eat there.

47
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:45,950
I can't do that.

48
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:48,710
What if he serves haggis and blood pudding?

49
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:52,900
I really doubt that's what he'll serve.

50
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:54,060
But what if he does?

51
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:55,600
I'll be obliged to dine

52
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:58,430
on liver and lungs stuffed in a sheep's stomach.

53
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:01,050
And frankly, blood pudding is essentially the same thing.

54
00:02:01,050 --> 00:02:02,980
I don't know why he's serving both.

55
00:02:04,190 --> 00:02:05,290
What do you want to do?

56
00:02:05,290 --> 00:02:07,330
You want to come with me, or do you want to sit here alone?

57
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:09,500
No, I'll go to your haggis party.

58
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,000
But I'm telling you.

59
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,470
This is adness. This is utter and complete adness.

60
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:42,420
Oh, dear!

61
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:44,780
- What? - Raj's television.

62
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:45,460
I just realized

63
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:48,160
we're about to spend an evening watching a plasma screen

64
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:51,410
with a cluster of dead pixels in the upper left-hand corner.

65
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:53,510
So don't watch TV.

66
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:54,590
Read a book.

67
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:55,940
And be a social pariah?

68
00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:57,750
Oh, you know that's not my style.

69
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:06,360
The audible sigh is a show of exasperation, right?

70
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:07,620
Right.

71
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:10,140
Is it about me or the dead pixels?

72
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:12,950
Hey, you're just in time.

73
00:03:12,950 --> 00:03:14,050
We made Tex-Mex.

74
00:03:14,050 --> 00:03:15,050
Oh, sounds great.

75
00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:17,430
Oh, Indians making Tex-Mex.

76
00:03:17,430 --> 00:03:19,380
Might as well have had the Chinese pizza.

77
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:22,400
Hey, you.

78
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,580
Hi.

79
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:27,370
That's got to be fun for you, huh?

80
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:30,960
Watching Hofstadter suck the saliva

81
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,700
out of your sister's mouth?

82
00:03:33,690 --> 00:03:35,910
Excuse me. Before this evening goes any further,

83
00:03:35,910 --> 00:03:38,520
we need to decide where everyone is going to sit.

84
00:03:39,710 --> 00:03:41,360
There is no assigned seats, Sheldon.

85
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,220
Just sit anywhere. Make yourself comfortable.

86
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,120
Oh, what fun.

87
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:47,390
We're like hippies at a love-in.

88
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:49,850
Just sit here.

89
00:03:49,850 --> 00:03:51,430
Right on, man. Right on.

90
00:03:54,610 --> 00:03:56,070
Oh, look.

91
00:03:56,070 --> 00:04:00,160
it's Harry Potter and 98% of The Sorcerer's Stone.

92
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:03,810
Okay, we've got fajitas

93
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:06,330
with all the fixins, so you make your own.

94
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:07,460
Wonderful.

95
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:09,620
Dinner, some assembly required.

96
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:13,060
Do you want a margarita, Sheldon?

97
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:13,790
A margarita?!

98
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:15,720
Where are we?! What is happening?!

99
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,650
Oh. Hey, Sheldon.

100
00:04:20,650 --> 00:04:21,850
What can I get you?

101
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:23,760
Water. Neat.

102
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:25,330
With a little umbrella.

103
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:27,980
Where are all your friends?

104
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:31,270
Sadly, Penny, this evening, I am the Dark Knight,

105
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:33,970
roaming these mean streets alone.

106
00:04:33,970 --> 00:04:36,100
A windbreaker for my cape,

107
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,690
and a stern expression for my cowl.

108
00:04:41,350 --> 00:04:42,650
Okay.

109
00:04:43,930 --> 00:04:45,190
Excuse me?

110
00:04:45,190 --> 00:04:47,920
Isn't this the point where the world-weary barkeep

111
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:49,810
absentmindedly wipes down the bar

112
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:53,050
and coaxes the woes out of the troubled patron?

113
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:56,930
Well, I was getting your stupid umbrella, but all right.

114
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,960
What's troubling you, buddy?

115
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:06,990
I don't think your heart's in it, but since you asked...

116
00:05:06,990 --> 00:05:10,270
Apparently, because Leonard is dating Raj's sister,

117
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:12,890
we're all forced to hang out at his apartment.

118
00:05:12,890 --> 00:05:14,500
Oh, the horror.

119
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:15,800
Indeed.

120
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:18,470
Yeah, at one point, Raj put on reggae music,

121
00:05:18,470 --> 00:05:21,040
and his sister took off her shoes.

122
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:23,650
It was like the last days of Caligula.

123
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:29,670
Oh, I have to get this.

124
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,750
Umbrella?

125
00:05:34,650 --> 00:05:36,680
Wonder what she's exasperated about.

126
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,190
Hello?

127
00:05:39,190 --> 00:05:40,680
Sheldon, are you all right?

128
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,990
When last we spoke, you were going to

129
00:05:41,990 --> 00:05:44,620
take a taxi home from Raj's, but according to Facebook,

130
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:46,460
you just checked in at the Cheesecake Factory.

131
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:48,310
Yes, I was in a taxi,

132
00:05:48,310 --> 00:05:50,410
but the driver didn't look at all

133
00:05:50,410 --> 00:05:52,210
like the photograph on his license,

134
00:05:52,210 --> 00:05:54,200
so I leapt out and ran for it.

135
00:05:55,090 --> 00:05:56,490
Wise.

136
00:05:56,710 --> 00:05:57,630
There you go.

137
00:05:57,630 --> 00:06:00,470
Just like recovering alcoholics drink in the Caribbean.

138
00:06:01,530 --> 00:06:02,960
Hi, bestie.

139
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,410
Oh. Hi, Amy.

140
00:06:04,410 --> 00:06:05,220
How you been?

141
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:06,540
Fine.

142
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:09,050
From this angle, I can see up your nose.

143
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:12,160
Yeah, it's a great time to be alive, isn't it?

144
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:14,240
Don't worry. My problems can wait

145
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,570
while you two hens finish your clucking.

146
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:19,660
Look, Sheldon, Leonard is dating Priya.

147
00:06:19,660 --> 00:06:20,860
She is staying with Raj.

148
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:23,990
That means you're all probably gonna be hanging out there more.

149
00:06:24,370 --> 00:06:26,560
Penny, I'm sorry you got dragged into this.

150
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,680
I know you're devastated

151
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,830
that your ex-boyfriend has found an exciting new lover

152
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:32,140
with flawless, caramel-colored skin.

153
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:35,850
Okay, I'm not upset about Leonard and Priya.

154
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:38,520
Your flaring nostrils indicate otherwise.

155
00:06:39,490 --> 00:06:41,030
Cluck-cluck-cluck.

156
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:43,950
Sheldon, look at me.

157
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:45,140
I think it's time

158
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:46,000
to face the fact

159
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,260
that Leonard is the nucleus of your social group.

160
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:50,260
Where he goes, the group goes.

161
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:51,570
Leonard the nucleus?

162
00:06:51,570 --> 00:06:53,130
That makes no sense.

163
00:06:53,130 --> 00:06:54,580
I'm the whimsical elf

164
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,680
that everyone looks to for a good time.

165
00:06:58,010 --> 00:07:00,020
I'm not saying that you're not fun.

166
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:02,480
You're the most fun person I know.

167
00:07:04,430 --> 00:07:06,690
A lot of people think I'm fun to be around.

168
00:07:07,230 --> 00:07:08,820
Don't be needy, bestie.

169
00:07:09,350 --> 00:07:11,590
That's probably part of what chased Leonard away.

170
00:07:13,290 --> 00:07:14,930
What I am saying, Sheldon,

171
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:17,180
is that your group is Leonard-centric.

172
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:19,710
If it were a town, it would be Leonardville.

173
00:07:19,710 --> 00:07:22,540
If it were an Islamic nation, Leonardstan.

174
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:24,600
If it were the birthplace of motion pictures,

175
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:27,190
we'd all be singing "Hooray for Leonardwood."

176
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,640
Ooh, I got one.

177
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,780
If you guys were a band,

178
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:32,340
you'd be called Leonard and the Leonards.

179
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:36,230
So needy.

180
00:07:40,110 --> 00:07:41,480
What you doing?

181
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,610
I'm setting out snacks.

182
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:46,360
You do realize everyone's eating at Raj's again tonight.

183
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:50,250
I didn't say the snacks were for you now, did I, Nosy Rosie?

184
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,510
You're having people over?

185
00:07:56,510 --> 00:07:59,420
Yes. Must be killing you wondering who.

186
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,900
Fine, I'll tell you.

187
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:03,170
Stuart from the comic bookstore,

188
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:04,940
Barry Kripke from the university,

189
00:08:04,940 --> 00:08:06,700
Penny's ex-boyfriend Zack

190
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:09,490
and TV's LeVar Burton.

191
00:08:11,290 --> 00:08:12,360
Really?

192
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,030
LeVar Burton's coming here?

193
00:08:14,030 --> 00:08:16,040
Possibly. I Tweeted him.

194
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:20,160
Okay, well, tell him I loved him on Star Trek.

195
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:23,600
Please, Leonard, stop trying to horn in on my new friends.

196
00:08:24,730 --> 00:08:26,330
Of course. Good night.

197
00:08:26,330 --> 00:08:28,040
- Leonard. - Yeah?

198
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:31,590
We had a good run, you and I.

199
00:08:34,310 --> 00:08:36,370
Okay.

200
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:39,360
But change is a part of life.

201
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:41,330
It certainly is.

202
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:42,810
Okay.

203
00:08:43,450 --> 00:08:45,110
I have guests coming.

204
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:47,610
I'm afraid I'm going to have to ask you to leave now.

205
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:51,470
I am leaving.

206
00:08:51,470 --> 00:08:53,600
Don't make this harder than it is, Leonard.

207
00:08:54,990 --> 00:08:55,780
Good-bye, Sheldon.

208
00:08:55,780 --> 00:08:57,720
And good-bye to you, sir.

209
00:09:05,090 --> 00:09:06,270
He'll be back.

210
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:08,380
Of course I'll be back. I live here!

211
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:24,440
Well, it would appear

212
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,960
LeVar Burton won't be joining us.

213
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:28,810
Let's get started.

214
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:31,320
I thought we'd begin by going around the room,

215
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,620
introducing ourselves

216
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:35,030
and saying a little bit about why we're here.

217
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:37,340
Okay. I'm Sheldon.

218
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:38,630
Uh, for regular readers

219
00:09:38,630 --> 00:09:40,740
of The New England Journal of High Energy Physics,

220
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:42,470
I need no introduction.

221
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,620
If you're not familiar with that publication,

222
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:46,920
there's a free copy in your goody bag.

223
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:52,130
Stuart?

224
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:55,670
Um... Hi. I'm Stuart.

225
00:09:55,670 --> 00:09:57,550
I run a comic bookstore,

226
00:09:57,550 --> 00:10:00,750
which for financial reasons, I'm currently living in.

227
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:06,670
I guess what I'm hoping for most out of tonight is a hot shower.

228
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:09,720
It's very nice, Stuart.

229
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,740
Zack?

230
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:12,920
I'm Zack, and I'm, uh...

231
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:15,490
uh...

232
00:10:17,270 --> 00:10:18,880
Could you come back to me?

233
00:10:19,670 --> 00:10:20,830
Of course.

234
00:10:21,850 --> 00:10:22,730
Barry?

235
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:23,830
I'm Barry Kwipke, and I'm here

236
00:10:23,830 --> 00:10:26,170
because you told me there was going to be a whaffle.

237
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,030
When is the whaffle?

238
00:10:30,030 --> 00:10:31,610
Patience, patience, Barry.

239
00:10:31,610 --> 00:10:32,510
The whaffle...

240
00:10:32,510 --> 00:10:36,060
The raffle is the grand finale

241
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:39,770
to an evening-long festival of fun and folly.

242
00:10:39,770 --> 00:10:42,340
- One more question... - Yes, you must be present to win.

243
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:44,980
Okay, I'm ready.

244
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:47,840
I'm Zach, and I'm, uh...

245
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:49,850
Oh, crap, why is this so hard?

246
00:10:54,790 --> 00:10:55,490
Oh, hey.

247
00:10:55,490 --> 00:10:57,260
- Hi. - Yo, P-dog.

248
00:10:58,310 --> 00:10:59,240
What's up?

249
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:01,790
We're here to kidnap you for a girls' night out.

250
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:05,550
Parenthetical: the term "Kidnap" is being used playfully.

251
00:11:06,030 --> 00:11:07,530
I kind of figured that.

252
00:11:07,530 --> 00:11:10,180
Good. Now put this pillowcase over your head.

253
00:11:12,010 --> 00:11:13,310
No.

254
00:11:13,310 --> 00:11:14,330
She used to be much more fun,

255
00:11:14,330 --> 00:11:16,280
until Leonard punched her in the heart.

256
00:11:19,070 --> 00:11:20,200
We just thought you might want to go out

257
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:22,610
and have a good time, maybe go dancing.

258
00:11:22,610 --> 00:11:25,250
Oh. Gee, thanks, but I'm not really in the mood.

259
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:27,030
You do understand that it will distract you

260
00:11:27,030 --> 00:11:29,290
from obsessing over the rich variety of sweet loving

261
00:11:29,290 --> 00:11:30,110
that your ex-boyfriend

262
00:11:30,110 --> 00:11:33,150
is currently receiving from the fiery jewel of Mumbai.

263
00:11:35,030 --> 00:11:35,780
Okay, look,

264
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:37,110
if I agree to go out with you guys,

265
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:40,620
will you promise to stop pestering me about Leonard and Priya?

266
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:41,930
- Yes. - Sure.

267
00:11:41,930 --> 00:11:43,770
All right. I'll go change. Come on in.

268
00:11:44,670 --> 00:11:45,840
If you'd have let me bring the chloroform,

269
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:48,110
we wouldn't have had to put up with all this jibber-jabber.

270
